PAGES={
'/terms':('Terms of Use',[
('Who provides HUDDLE',f'HUDDLE is a product of {COMPANY}, GSTIN 33AAGCT9408C1ZI, at {ADDRESS}. These terms govern our digital business card platform, web application and Android application. An agreed Enterprise order may add commercial terms; it cannot remove mandatory legal rights.'),
('Accounts and authority','Use HUDDLE only if you are at least 18 and capable of entering a contract. Keep your account information accurate and your credentials secure. If you create or administer an organization, you confirm that you are authorized to act for it. Owners manage subscriptions; Owners and Admins manage members within their permissions. Do not share account access or attempt to access another organization’s private data.'),
('Cards, content and contact exchange','You remain responsible for the information, images, logos and links you publish and for having the rights and permissions to use them. Public card content is visible to anyone with its link, QR code or NFC tag and may be copied or indexed. A recipient chooses whether to submit details back. Organizations must use captured contacts only for lawful purposes consistent with their notice and consent; an exchange is not permission for unrelated bulk marketing.'),
('Subscriptions, trials and prices','New organizations start Free. Eligible Owners may start the trial shown in the application; the current Pro trial lasts 14 days and does not automatically take payment. Free limits apply after the trial unless a subscription or access grant is active. Published prices identify the billing cycle and included allowances. Applicable taxes are disclosed before payment. Enterprise is quoted separately and is not an automatic per-seat online purchase. Roadmap features are not part of a current purchase unless expressly agreed in writing.'),
('Payment and renewal','Where enabled, payment is processed by Razorpay or the payment provider shown at checkout. Paid access starts only after payment is verified. Renewal details, amount and billing interval must be reviewed before authorizing a recurring subscription. Stop future renewal from Upgrade & billing or request help at our support email. Cancellation normally takes effect at the end of the paid period. Existing contracts keep their agreed price unless lawfully changed with notice and any required consent.'),
('Refunds and separate hardware','Our Cancellation & Refunds Policy forms part of these terms. Paid software access is generally non-refundable for change of mind after activation, subject to the exceptions and mandatory rights in that policy. NFC cards, customization, taxes and shipping are not included in a digital subscription unless the order expressly includes them. A hardware enquiry is not a confirmed order; availability, artwork approval, total price and delivery terms must be agreed before payment.'),
('Acceptable use','Do not impersonate people, publish unlawful or infringing material, collect contacts deceptively, send spam, distribute malware, bypass plan limits, scrape private data or test security without permission. We may restrict access proportionately for misuse, security threats, legal obligations or unpaid access, and provide notice where appropriate and lawful. Contact support if you believe a restriction is mistaken.'),
('Ownership and service availability','You retain ownership of your content. You give us permission to host, display and process it only as needed to provide the service and its sharing features. HUDDLE software, branding and original materials remain ours or our licensors’. We aim for reliable operation but do not promise uninterrupted service or a specific service level unless agreed. Customers should export important contacts and avoid relying on the service as their only record.'),
('Third-party links and NFC','WhatsApp, UPI apps, linked websites and payment providers operate under their own terms. HUDDLE does not process UPI transfers between card visitors and card owners. NFC use depends on compatible devices, tags, internet access and a reachable profile URL; we do not guarantee every device or tag works. Deactivating a link does not erase information already saved by a recipient.'),
('Responsibility and mandatory rights','Each party remains responsible for its own conduct and obligations under applicable law. We do not exclude liability or remedies that cannot lawfully be excluded, including applicable consumer protections. Do not treat marketing statements, illustrative environmental estimates or roadmap descriptions as guarantees of sales results, measured tree savings or release dates.'),
('Closure, changes and disputes',f'You may request account closure and assistance with your data at {EMAIL}; we may verify your authority and retain records required for legal, financial, security or dispute purposes. We will publish material policy changes with an updated date and provide additional notice where required. Indian law applies, subject to mandatory protections and competent courts or consumer forums. Raise concerns with us first at {EMAIL}; this does not prevent access to statutory remedies.')]),
'/privacy':('Privacy Policy',[
('Scope and responsibility',f'{COMPANY} operates HUDDLE. This policy covers huddleapp.in and associated application and service domains. We handle account, service-operation, billing and sales-enquiry information. An organization also determines how its members’ profiles and captured contacts are used; contact that organization about its own processing. We process organization data to provide the service and under the applicable customer arrangement.'),
('Information we collect','Depending on what you use, this includes name and email, account credentials in protected form, organization and role, profile contact details, photos and banners, card and NFC assignments, details voluntarily submitted through contact exchanges, sales-enquiry requirements and contact consent, subscription and payment reference/status information, activity events, security and operational logs, authentication/session information and essential browser storage. We do not ask for UPI PINs, card PINs or banking passwords. Avoid putting sensitive personal information in public cards or enquiry messages.'),
('Why we use it','We use information to authenticate accounts; provide, share and manage cards; administer organizations and permissions; deliver consented contact exchanges; show networking activity; enforce plan limits; respond to enquiries and support; operate billing; prevent abuse; investigate incidents and comply with applicable law. We rely on consent or other grounds permitted by applicable law as appropriate. A sales-enquiry consent covers replying to that enquiry, not unrelated promotional mailing.'),
('Public and shared information','A published card is intended to be shared. Anyone with the URL, QR code or NFC link may see the fields published on it and save a contact file. Card owners and authorized organization administrators may see contact details a recipient submits back and the associated activity allowed by their roles. Do not publish information you wish to keep private. Changing or deleting a profile does not withdraw copies already downloaded by others.'),
('No sale of personal data','We do not sell personal data or provide it to data brokers. We do not share private contact lists with unrelated businesses for their independent advertising. Operational disclosures to service providers, authorized organization users and legally required recipients are described here; they are not a sale of your data.'),
('Service providers and lawful disclosures','We use Vercel for hosting and Supabase for database and file storage. Razorpay handles payments when configured. Resend may deliver service emails when enabled; Google sign-in may be available when configured. These providers receive only information needed for their service, under applicable arrangements. We may disclose information when legally required, to protect users and the service, or in a lawful business transfer with appropriate safeguards and notice. Third-party links and payment pages have their own privacy policies.'),
('Cookies, storage and analytics','Essential session cookies and browser storage support sign-in, security and application preferences. Networking activity is used to provide card and team analytics; it does not establish that a downloaded contact was imported into an address book or that an NFC physical tap has been independently verified. We do not use this notice as consent to non-essential advertising trackers. If such tracking is introduced, we will update the notice and seek any required consent.'),
('Storage, retention and security','We use access controls, organization scoping, protected credentials and encrypted connections where supported to reduce risk. No system is risk-free. Data may be processed in the locations used by our configured service providers, which may include locations outside India. We retain information for the purposes described here and applicable legal, accounting, security and dispute requirements. Retention depends on the record and purpose; no universal seven-day auto-deletion applies. Account closure or deletion requests are reviewed with authorization checks and applicable retention exceptions. Backup copies may persist through their rotation cycle.'),
('Your choices and requests',f'You can update permitted profile fields, deactivate cards where your role allows, stop sharing a public link and decline contact exchange. To request access, correction, deletion, withdrawal of consent or grievance assistance, email {EMAIL} with the subject “HUDDLE Privacy”. We may verify identity and organization authority and explain any legal or technical limit. Withdrawing consent does not undo prior lawful processing and may affect features that require the information. You may pursue remedies available under applicable Indian law.'),
('Children and updates','HUDDLE accounts are intended for adults aged 18 or over. We do not knowingly invite children to create accounts or submit personal data. Contact us if you believe a child’s information has been submitted. We will review the concern and take appropriate action. We update this notice when practices change and provide additional notice or consent choices where required.'),
('Contact',f'Privacy and grievance correspondence: {EMAIL}, subject “HUDDLE Privacy / Grievance”. Write to {COMPANY}, {ADDRESS}. This policy describes our practices; it does not claim certification or regulatory approval.')]),
'/data-protection':('Data Protection',[
('Our commitments','HUDDLE is built to separate organizations and restrict actions by role. We do not sell personal data or private lead lists. This page explains the service’s data-handling approach; it is not a security certification, independent audit or a substitute for an Enterprise data-processing agreement.'),
('Your organization’s control','Organization Owners and authorized administrators manage membership, branding and access. Members can manage their permitted profile fields. Customers must establish a lawful basis for the data they upload and the contacts they collect, give appropriate notices and respect withdrawal and deletion requests. Public card fields are deliberately shared and should be kept to professional information.'),
('How we protect access','The application uses authenticated sessions, server-side permissions and organization checks for private operations. Sensitive platform administration requires separate elevated access and MFA. Credentials and authenticator secrets are protected, and private uploaded images are served through controlled application paths. Publicly published images and profile details remain accessible as part of the card experience.'),
('Providers, incidents and requests',f'Hosting, storage and payment providers are identified in our Privacy Policy. We assess incidents, take appropriate containment steps and provide notifications where required by applicable law or contract. To report suspected exposure or request a data-processing agreement for Enterprise, email {EMAIL}. Do not send passwords, payment credentials or unnecessary personal information in a report.'),
('Retention and deletion','We retain records according to their operational purpose and applicable obligations, rather than promising immediate deletion from every system. Verified deletion requests may require coordination with the customer organization and may be subject to legal retention, security logs and backup rotation. A downloaded contact or a recipient’s independent copy is outside HUDDLE’s direct control.')]),
'/refunds':('Cancellation & Refunds',[
('Try before you subscribe','Eligible organization Owners can use the 14-day Pro trial shown in the application before choosing a paid subscription. The trial does not automatically charge a payment method. At trial expiry, Free limits apply unless separate paid access or a grant is active. Review the package, billing cycle, limits and checkout total before paying.'),
('Cancel future renewal',f'Owners can request cancellation from Upgrade & billing where recurring billing is enabled, or contact {EMAIL} for assistance. Cancellation normally stops future renewal at the end of the current paid period; it does not automatically refund elapsed or unused time. Check the confirmation and payment-provider status. A provider-processed payment already due may need separate review.'),
('Software refund policy','We generally do not provide change-of-mind refunds or prorated refunds for unused time after paid access has been activated. This does not exclude refunds or remedies for duplicate payments, incorrect charges, a paid service that was not supplied as agreed, or rights that apply under law. We review such cases on their facts; the availability of a free trial does not waive mandatory rights.'),
('NFC orders','Physical NFC cards are separate from subscriptions. Before a hardware order is paid, the written quote must state cancellation, customization, returns and delivery terms. Personalized cards may not qualify for change-of-mind returns after approved production begins; defective, damaged, incorrect or undelivered goods and mandatory legal remedies are not excluded. A hardware enquiry alone creates no order or payment obligation.'),
('Request a review',f'Email {EMAIL} with the account email, organization, payment reference, date and reason. Do not send a full card number, CVV, UPI PIN or banking password. We verify the transaction and respond with the outcome and any refund-processing information. Approved refunds are normally returned to the original payment method through the payment provider; bank/provider settlement times vary. Enterprise agreements may contain additional terms, subject to applicable law.')]),
'/shipping':('Delivery & Shipping',[
('Digital service delivery','Digital cards are accessed through a browser; no physical shipment is needed for software subscriptions. New paid access is enabled after verified payment. Pending, failed or disputed payment may delay activation. Contact support with your reference if payment succeeded but access did not update.'),
('Optional physical NFC cards','NFC hardware, branding and shipping are separate from the digital subscription unless expressly included in an accepted quote. Hardware is supplied only after availability, quantity, material, artwork approval, destination, full price and delivery terms are confirmed. The website enquiry form does not place an order.'),
('Before paying for hardware','Your written order confirmation must state dispatch estimates, delivery charges, applicable taxes, delivery areas and the process for damaged, wrong or missing items. We do not currently promise a standard dispatch window, free delivery or worldwide shipping. Delays and courier issues are handled under the agreed order terms and applicable law.'),
('Support',f'For activation or hardware delivery enquiries, contact {EMAIL}. Quote your account or order reference; avoid including unnecessary personal or payment information.')]),
'/contact':('Contact HUDDLE',[
('Customer support',f'Email {EMAIL} for product help, billing, cancellation, NFC enquiries or account requests. Include the account email, organization and a short explanation; do not include passwords, OTPs, CVVs or UPI PINs.'),
('Privacy and grievances',f'Email {EMAIL} with the subject “HUDDLE Privacy / Grievance”. We may verify identity and authority before acting on an account or organization request.'),
('Legal business details',f'{COMPANY}. A Product of Touchmark Descience Pvt Ltd. Registered business address supplied by the company: {ADDRESS}. GSTIN: 33AAGCT9408C1ZI. State: Tamil Nadu. Product domain: huddleapp.in.'),
('Sales','For software team plans use our Enterprise quote form. For optional physical hardware use the NFC cards enquiry page. An enquiry does not create a purchase or subscription.')]),
'/about':('About HUDDLE',[
('A Product of Touchmark Descience Pvt Ltd','HUDDLE helps individuals and organizations share professional profiles through links, QR codes and optional reusable NFC cards. Recipients need only a browser to view a shared card.'),
('Digital first, hardware optional','The service offers card templates, organization branding and member controls, consent-based contact exchange and networking activity, according to your package. Compatible NFC hardware is optional and quoted separately. Apple/Google Wallet passes, direct CRM integrations and an iOS app remain planned rather than included operational services.'),
('Our company',f'HUDDLE is operated by {COMPANY}, {ADDRESS}. GSTIN: 33AAGCT9408C1ZI. Contact: {EMAIL}. The payment gateway and other providers may require their own account activation; this page is not a claim of Razorpay approval.')])}

def page(path):
    title,sections=PAGES[path]
    nav=''.join(f'<a href="{escape(url)}" {"aria-current=page" if url==path else ""}>{escape(name)}</a>' for url,(name,_) in PAGES.items())
    body=''.join(f'<section><h2>{escape(h)}</h2><p>{escape(t)}</p></section>' for h,t in sections)
    return f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>{escape(title)} · HUDDLE</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/static/brand-theme.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/static/legal.css"></head><body><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header><a class="brand" href="/"><b>h*</b> huddle.</a><a href="/pricing">Pricing</a><a href="/nfc-cards">NFC cards</a><a href="/app/login">Sign in ↗</a></header><main id="main"><p class="kicker">A Product of Touchmark Descience Pvt Ltd</p><h1>{escape(title)}</h1><p class="updated">Last updated: {UPDATED}</p><nav aria-label="Company and policies">{nav}</nav><article>{body}</article><aside><strong>{COMPANY}</strong><p>{ADDRESS}<br>GSTIN: 33AAGCT9408C1ZI<br><a href="mailto:{EMAIL}">{EMAIL}</a></p></aside></main><footer>HUDDLE · huddleapp.in · <a href="/enterprise#request-quote">Enterprise enquiries</a></footer></body></html>'''
